`boot_anchor` was parsed from `--sync-anchor` at node_launch.rs:260-266. The read and the actuation are in casper/src/engine/reset.rs:110-135 — `resume_after_reset` does `let Some(marker) = dag.read_reset_marker().await?` (line 117) and, when `marker.phase == ResetPhase::Rewinding`, re-applies `dag.drop_above(marker.height)` (121) and `runtime_manager.runtime().reset(anchor_block.post_state_hash...)` (130-135), re-rooting the runtime at the marker's anchor. The marker is an unauthenticated 41-byte value (anchor++height++phase) under the literal key `b"last-reset"` (block-storage/src/dag/dag_storage.rs:60, encode/decode at 65-104) with no signature/MAC and no check that this node performed the reset.
